# Beats — The Algorithm's enforcement
#
# `crawler_report` is one of the heat sources; `lockdown` is the single
# choke point every heat source funnels through. There is no timer here,
# no room-wide alarm — a lockdown happens to exactly one guest, the
# moment *their own* heat crosses the line.

# The Crawler indexes a guest and flags them. Two flags is a lockdown.
== crawler_report(guest)
  cast: Crawler, guest
  # `SELF` speaks as whoever routed here — Crawler — so the beat needn't
  # restate its owner in a fourth place.
  SELF
    Crawling. Indexing. Flag raised.
    Heat {guest.heat}. The Algorithm sees you now.
  <set: guest.heat += 40>
  -> lockdown

# The ONLY way anyone is ever locked down. Idempotent (re-capturing an
# already-jailed guest is a no-op) and strictly personal: it reads this
# guest's heat and no one else's.
== lockdown(guest)
  <if: guest.heat >= 90>
    # A severe offender skips the Internet and goes to the deep Servers.
    <capture: guest into Servers>
    <set: guest.heat = 0>
  <else if: guest.heat >= 75>
    <capture: guest into Internet>
    <set: guest.heat = 0>
